{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772650951,"nonce":"HdXUL4z7nOa1QG3aaUz925A4WqE=","title":"TypeScript build: worktrees report 200+ errors, main worktree reports 0","message":"When running `tsc` or `npm run build` inside a Mandible feature worktree, TypeScript reports ~217 errors (primarily `module not found`, `NodeJS namespace not found`, `Buffer not found`). The same build in the main worktree reports 0 errors.\n\n**Root cause:** Feature worktrees do not have `node_modules/` installed. `@types/node` and other type packages are missing.\n\n**Fix options:**\n1. In `.worktree.yaml`, add `node_modules` to the shared symlinks list (with appropriate exclusions to avoid the `npm ci` corruption issue)\n2. Add a post-`wt` hook that runs `npm install` (or copies node_modules) in the new worktree\n\n**Status:** Fixed in dotfiles retro-fixes branch. This issue tracks the fix landing in the standalone repo.\n\nMigrated from dotfiles issue 901c4a3.","files":null}]}